    "/v1/usage": {
      "get": {
        "summary": "Get plan usage",
        "description": "The workspace's plan, emails used this billing period, what a send would be refused for right now, and what the period costs so far. Call it before a large batch or campaign rather than discovering a limit halfway through. sending_locked and lock_reason are the fields worth branching on: they name the exact 402 a send would answer with, including payment_method_required, which no API caller can resolve — a person has to add a payment method in the dashboard. The count trails real sending, so leave headroom rather than sending exactly emails_remaining. Takes no parameters.",
