      "post": {
        "summary": "Create an automation",
        "description": "Created as a draft; POST /v1/automations/{id}/status with active turns it on. Prefer a sequence over scheduling several emails yourself: it ends on its own when the person unsubscribes, replies, is suppressed, opts out of its topic, or their tags say so. The definition is checked now rather than at the first send: from and identity_id against a verified marketing domain, topic_key, a contact_added trigger's audience_id, and every step's body or template_slug. A 422 here is a definition to fix, not something to retry unchanged. For api and event triggers placeholder values are not checked, because they arrive with each enrolment: a missing one fails that enrolment when the step comes due. contact_added and tag_added enrol with none, so their placeholders must all be covered by default_variables.",
        "x-required-scope": "broadcasts:write",
        "requestBody": {
