      "post": {
        "summary": "Create a campaign",
        "description": "Creates a draft. Nothing is sent and nothing about the audience is resolved until POST /v1/broadcasts/{id}/send; run GET /v1/broadcasts/{id}/preview first to see who it would reach. audience_id, identity_id and segment_id take ids, not names: a name answers 422 with the id to use, so read the message and retry with that id rather than another spelling. The sending domain must be a marketing one, so a campaign's complaints can never touch password resets. Pass 'variants' to make it an A/B test over subject, from_name or send_at: the sample goes out, the campaign sits in 'testing', and after decide_after_minutes the variant with the best unique open (or click) rate gets the rest. Every variant needs at least 100 recipients in the sample or the send fails. A 422 is a problem with the body: fix it, do not retry unchanged.",
        "x-required-scope": "broadcasts:write",
        "requestBody": {
          "required": true,
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/CreateBroadcastRequest"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "201": {
            "description": "The draft, with every field present (null for what was not given) and 'warnings' when a setting will not do what it says yet.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Broadcast"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "400": {
            "description": "invalid_json: the request body is not valid JSON.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "401": {
            "description": "unauthorized: no Bearer token, or the key or token is invalid, revoked or expired.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "403": {
            "description": "forbidden: the key lacks the broadcasts:write scope. The message names it.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "409": {
            "description": "idempotency_in_progress: a request with the same Idempotency-Key was still running on this path after waiting up to 8 seconds for it (a retry that finds it finished receives its response instead). Retry after a short wait.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "413": {
            "description": "payload_too_large: the body is larger than this endpoint accepts (5 MB unless stated).",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "422": {
            "description": "invalid_request: a field fails the schema ('Validation failed', with details; for from_name the rule broken); audience_id, identity_id or segment_id is not an id in your workspace (the message starts with the field name and gives the id when the value is a name); identity_id is a transactional domain; segment_id filters a different audience; or the A/B settings break a rule (ab_test without variants, a bad or repeated key, an empty variant subject, send_at on some variants but not all, sample_share outside 0.05 to 1, decide_after_minutes outside 15 to 10080). unknown_topic: topic_key names no topic in your workspace (message starts \"topic_key:\"). Also idempotency_key_reused: this Idempotency-Key was already used on this path with a different request body (checked right after the scope, so a credential without the scope gets 403 instead, and answered at once even while the first request is still running). Do not retry; send the new request under a new key.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "429": {
            "description": "rate_limited: more requests than the per-key rate (600 a minute by default). Wait the seconds in the Retry-After header and retry.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "503": {
            "description": "service_unavailable: the API is under heavy load and could not get a database connection in time. Usually nothing was done; a send that was already under way may have been, so check GET /v1/emails before retrying one. Wait the seconds in the Retry-After header.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "Idempotency-Key",
            "in": "header",
            "schema": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "description": "Replaying the same key on the same path in this workspace within 24 hours returns the stored response, with an Idempotent-Replay: true header, instead of acting again. Only successful responses are stored, so a failed request can be fixed and retried under the same key. The body is compared (key order ignored): the same key with a different body is 422 idempotency_key_reused, so use a new key for every new request. Use an unguessable value such as a UUID."
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "/v1/broadcasts/{id}": {
      "get": {
        "summary": "Get a campaign",
        "description": "One campaign; the call to poll after a send. While it is sending, paused or testing it carries a 'progress' object counted from the frozen audience, which tells a campaign still draining from one that is waiting. When paused, read pause_reason and resume_after before calling resume. For an A/B test that has left draft, 'ab_test.results' holds live per-variant figures.",
        "x-required-scope": "broadcasts:read",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "id",
            "in": "path",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "type": "string",
              "format": "uuid"
            },
            "description": "The campaign's id from POST or GET /v1/broadcasts (a UUID), not its name."
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "The campaign.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Broadcast"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "401": {
            "description": "unauthorized: no Bearer token, or the key or token is invalid, revoked or expired.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "403": {
            "description": "forbidden: the key lacks the broadcasts:read scope. The message names it.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "not_found: no campaign with this id in your workspace. When the value is a campaign's name, the message gives its id.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "429": {
            "description": "rate_limited: more requests than the per-key rate (600 a minute by default). Wait the seconds in the Retry-After header and retry.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "503": {
            "description": "service_unavailable: the API is under heavy load and could not get a database connection in time. Usually nothing was done; a send that was already under way may have been, so check GET /v1/emails before retrying one. Wait the seconds in the Retry-After header.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "patch": {
        "summary": "Update a campaign",
        "description": "Edits a draft, or moves or unschedules a scheduled campaign. A draft accepts name, subject, html, from_name, variants and ab_test; the audience, domain, segment and topic are fixed (delete and recreate to change them), and scheduled_at is refused (schedule a draft with POST /v1/broadcasts/{id}/send). A scheduled campaign accepts a body of only scheduled_at: a new time moves it, null returns it to draft so it can be edited; any other body answers 409, so unschedule first. A scheduled_at other than null from an API key that holds its sends for approval or has allowed_recipients is 403 forbidden, checked before the campaign's status and the value itself; such a key may still unschedule with null. A new scheduled_at earlier than the stored one, from a key with a daily_send_limit that has not paid for the campaign, counts what it still has to send against the key (429 daily_limit when that does not fit today). Nothing else is editable once a campaign has started. variants and ab_test travel together: ab_test alone merges over the stored settings and variants; variants alone replaces the list and keeps the settings.",
        "x-required-scope": "broadcasts:write",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "id",
            "in": "path",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "type": "string",
              "format": "uuid"
            },
            "description": "The campaign's id from POST or GET /v1/broadcasts (a UUID), not its name."
          }
        ],
        "requestBody": {
          "required": true,
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/UpdateBroadcastRequest"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "The campaign read back from storage (unset fields read null), with 'warnings' when a setting will not do what it says yet. After a scheduled_at change it shows the new status and scheduled_at.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Broadcast"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "400": {
            "description": "invalid_json: the request body is not valid JSON.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "401": {
            "description": "unauthorized: no Bearer token, or the key or token is invalid, revoked or expired.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "403": {
            "description": "forbidden: the calling API key holds its sends for approval (a campaign cannot be held for approval), or has allowed_recipients (a campaign's audience cannot be held to an allowlist). The message says which. Use a key without that guardrail, or send the campaign from the dashboard; retrying with this key will not help. Only for a body with a scheduled_at other than null, whatever the campaign's status and whether or not the value is valid; null is allowed. Also forbidden: the key lacks the broadcasts:write scope. The message names it.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "not_found: no campaign with this id in your workspace, or it was deleted while a new scheduled_at was being applied.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "409": {
            "description": "invalid_state: the campaign is neither a draft nor a scheduled campaign given only scheduled_at (the message names its status); scheduled_at: null on a campaign that has already run (or that a run claimed, or that was deleted, meanwhile); or a run claimed it while a new scheduled_at was being applied. Read the campaign before retrying.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "413": {
            "description": "payload_too_large: the body is larger than this endpoint accepts (5 MB unless stated).",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "422": {
            "description": "invalid_request: a field fails the schema ('Validation failed', with details); scheduled_at on a draft; a new scheduled_at on a send-time A/B test; or the A/B settings break a rule, as on create ('ab_test needs variants' for ab_test alone on a campaign with none).",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "429": {
            "description": "daily_limit: a new scheduled_at earlier than the campaign's current time, from an API key with a daily_send_limit that has not paid for this campaign, and what the campaign still has to send would take the key past today's limit. Nothing changes. Also rate_limited: more requests than the per-key rate (600 a minute by default). Wait the seconds in the Retry-After header and retry.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "503": {
            "description": "service_unavailable: the API is under heavy load and could not get a database connection in time. Usually nothing was done; a send that was already under way may have been, so check GET /v1/emails before retrying one. Wait the seconds in the Retry-After header.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "delete": {
        "summary": "Delete a campaign",
        "description": "Deletes the campaign and its frozen audience, in every status except 'sending'. A scheduled campaign is removed, not returned to draft (PATCH scheduled_at: null does that). Deleting is also the only way to abandon a paused campaign: for a paused or testing one, everyone still pending is discarded (for a test, the whole remainder waiting for the winner), and it can never be resumed. Messages already sent stay in the email log, but the campaign's recipients and clicked links are no longer reachable. Cannot be undone.",
