    "/v1/broadcasts/{id}/send": {
      "post": {
        "summary": "Send or schedule a campaign",
        "description": "Starts a draft or scheduled campaign now (empty body), schedules a draft, or moves a scheduled campaign (scheduled_at). A send mails everyone the preview counts and cannot be recalled: run GET /v1/broadcasts/{id}/preview first. Refused with 422 when the workspace has no postal address (marketing mail must carry one, with a visible unsubscribe link) or its sending is suspended, whether starting now or scheduling; both are checked again at start and before every batch, where they pause the campaign instead. Starting now answers 202 'sending' at once and runs in the background: the reputation gate, the sending domain (verified, marketing), the plan allowance and the A/B sample floor are checked by the run and, if they fail, leave the campaign 'failed' with failure_reason rather than returning an error here, so poll GET /v1/broadcasts/{id}. The campaign ends 'sent', 'testing' once an A/B sample is out, or 'paused' on warm-up, quota or throttling. A scheduled campaign is started by the worker after its time (it checks every 30 seconds, one due start per check, so a start can lag). A send-time A/B test takes no scheduled_at: it is scheduled at its earliest variant's send_at, and calling send again on one already scheduled changes nothing and returns the stored time. The calling API key's guardrails apply: a key that holds its sends for approval or has allowed_recipients cannot send, schedule or reschedule a campaign (403). A key with a daily_send_limit is charged once for each campaign it puts on its way, whoever scheduled it: sending or scheduling a draft counts the audience as it resolves now, and starting a scheduled campaign now or moving it earlier counts what it still has to send, unless this key already paid for the campaign; when that does not fit what is left of today's limit the call is 429 daily_limit. Moving a campaign later counts nothing. OAuth tokens and keys without guardrails are unaffected. Checks run in the order: the campaign exists (404), key guardrails (403), campaign status (409), body (422), postal address and suspension (422), daily limit (429).",
        "x-required-scope": "broadcasts:write",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "id",
            "in": "path",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "type": "string",
              "format": "uuid"
            },
            "description": "The campaign's id from POST or GET /v1/broadcasts (a UUID), not its name."
          },
          {
            "name": "Idempotency-Key",
            "in": "header",
            "schema": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "description": "Replaying the same key on the same path in this workspace within 24 hours returns the stored response, with an Idempotent-Replay: true header, instead of acting again. Only successful responses are stored, so a failed request can be fixed and retried under the same key. The body is compared (key order ignored): the same key with a different body is 422 idempotency_key_reused, so use a new key for every new request. Use an unguessable value such as a UUID."
          }
        ],
        "requestBody": {
          "required": false,
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/SendBroadcastRequest"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "202": {
            "description": "The campaign object, as retrieve returns it. Started now, its status is 'sending' (the run claims it in the background; a very fast run may already show where it ended). Scheduled, it is 'scheduled' with scheduled_at as stored: for a send-time test the earliest variant's send_at, or the next variant's between variants.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Broadcast"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "400": {
            "description": "invalid_json: the request body is not valid JSON.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "401": {
            "description": "unauthorized: no Bearer token, or the key or token is invalid, revoked or expired.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "403": {
            "description": "forbidden: the calling API key holds its sends for approval (a campaign cannot be held for approval), or has allowed_recipients (a campaign's audience cannot be held to an allowlist). The message says which. Use a key without that guardrail, or send the campaign from the dashboard; retrying with this key will not help. Also forbidden: the key lacks the broadcasts:write scope. The message names it.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "not_found: no campaign with this id in your workspace, or it was deleted while being scheduled.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "409": {
            "description": "invalid_state: the campaign is not draft or scheduled ('Broadcast is already <status>'), or a run claimed it while it was being scheduled. Do not retry; read the campaign. Also idempotency_in_progress: a request with the same Idempotency-Key was still running on this path after waiting up to 8 seconds for it (a retry that finds it finished receives its response instead). Retry after a short wait.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "413": {
            "description": "payload_too_large: the body is larger than this endpoint accepts (5 MB unless stated).",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "422": {
            "description": "no_postal_address: the workspace has no postal address; add one in Settings, then retry. workspace_suspended: sending is suspended for the workspace; do not retry. invalid_request: scheduled_at is not a UTC ISO 8601 timestamp ('Bad scheduled_at'), or scheduled_at was given for a send-time A/B test. Also idempotency_key_reused: this Idempotency-Key was already used on this path with a different request body (checked right after the scope, so a credential without the scope gets 403 instead, and answered at once even while the first request is still running). Do not retry; send the new request under a new key.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "429": {
            "description": "daily_limit: an API key with a daily_send_limit sending or scheduling a draft, or, when it has not paid for this campaign, starting a scheduled campaign now or moving it earlier, and the recipients would take the key past today's limit. The message gives both numbers. Do not retry today with this key; it resets at 00:00 UTC. Also rate_limited: more requests than the per-key rate (600 a minute by default). Wait the seconds in the Retry-After header and retry.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "503": {
            "description": "service_unavailable: the API is under heavy load and could not get a database connection in time. Usually nothing was done; a send that was already under way may have been, so check GET /v1/emails before retrying one. Wait the seconds in the Retry-After header.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/v1/broadcasts/{id}/resume": {
      "post": {
        "summary": "Resume a paused campaign",
        "description": "Continues a 'paused' campaign now instead of waiting for the worker. It mails only addresses still pending in the frozen audience, each claimed before it is sent, so calling it twice, or while the worker is resuming too, never mails anyone twice. An A/B test paused during its sample resumes the sample; one paused after the decision resumes the winner. Read pause_reason first, because what continues a pause depends on its cause. Warm-up: resume_after is set, this call answers 409 until then, and the worker resumes it on its own after it; the ramp is protecting the domain, so wait. 24-hour quota: the worker resumes it when the window frees; resuming while it is still spent is accepted with 202 but sends nothing and pauses again. Throttling or an interrupted run: the worker resumes it on its next check. No postal address: this call answers 422 until one is added in Settings, and then the worker resumes it on its own. Suspension: this call answers 422 while suspended, and once the suspension is lifted the worker resumes it on its own. The 202 does not mean mail went out: every run re-checks the reputation gate and the sending domain, suppressions and topic opt-outs, and can end the campaign 'failed'. Poll GET /v1/broadcasts/{id} for progress. An API key that holds its sends for approval or has allowed_recipients cannot resume a campaign (403, checked before the campaign's status). A key with a daily_send_limit that has not paid for the campaign is charged for the addresses still pending (429 daily_limit when they do not fit today).",
        "x-required-scope": "broadcasts:write",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "id",
            "in": "path",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "type": "string",
              "format": "uuid"
            },
            "description": "The campaign's id from POST or GET /v1/broadcasts (a UUID), not its name."
          },
          {
            "name": "Idempotency-Key",
            "in": "header",
            "schema": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "description": "Replaying the same key on the same path in this workspace within 24 hours returns the stored response, with an Idempotent-Replay: true header, instead of acting again. Only successful responses are stored, so a failed request can be fixed and retried under the same key. The body is compared (key order ignored): the same key with a different body is 422 idempotency_key_reused, so use a new key for every new request. Use an unguessable value such as a UUID."
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "202": {
            "description": "The campaign object, status 'sending', with progress.pending the addresses still to send. For an A/B test paused during its sample that includes the remainder waiting for the winner, which this run does not send.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Broadcast"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "400": {
            "description": "invalid_json: the request body is not valid JSON.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "401": {
            "description": "unauthorized: no Bearer token, or the key or token is invalid, revoked or expired.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "403": {
            "description": "forbidden: the calling API key holds its sends for approval (a campaign cannot be held for approval), or has allowed_recipients (a campaign's audience cannot be held to an allowlist). The message says which. Use a key without that guardrail, or send the campaign from the dashboard; retrying with this key will not help. Also forbidden: the key lacks the broadcasts:write scope. The message names it.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "not_found: no campaign with this id in your workspace.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "409": {
            "description": "invalid_state: the campaign is not paused (the message names its status), or it is paused on warm-up and its allowance has not renewed (the message gives the time; the worker resumes it then, so do not retry before it). Also idempotency_in_progress: a request with the same Idempotency-Key was still running on this path after waiting up to 8 seconds for it (a retry that finds it finished receives its response instead). Retry after a short wait.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "413": {
            "description": "payload_too_large: the body is larger than this endpoint accepts (5 MB unless stated).",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "422": {
            "description": "no_postal_address: the workspace has no postal address; add one in Settings. workspace_suspended: sending is suspended for the workspace. Both are checked before the warm-up refusal. Also idempotency_key_reused: this Idempotency-Key was already used on this path with a different request body (checked right after the scope, so a credential without the scope gets 403 instead, and answered at once even while the first request is still running). Do not retry; send the new request under a new key.",
            "content": {
