      "delete": {
        "summary": "Remove suppressions from many addresses",
        "description": "Lifts the suppression with exactly this scope from up to 10,000 addresses; the body goes in the DELETE request. Removing scope all leaves a marketing suppression in place. Removal does not check the reason: lifting a hard_bounce or complaint re-enables mail to a dead mailbox or to someone who reported spam, which raises the rates AWS pauses accounts on. Never lift suppressions to work around failed sends.",
